cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ZoomzPeak: an ontology-anchored Parquet format for ZooMS and palaeoproteomics data"
message: "If you use this specification or software, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  ZoomzPeak defines mzPeakMS-ZooMS, a profile of the HUPO-PSI mzPeak format for
  ZooMS (Zooarchaeology by Mass Spectrometry) and palaeoproteomics data. It binds
  the measurement half of the data to the PSI-MS controlled vocabulary and the
  archaeological half to published archaeological ontologies, and provides
  reference builders and a conformance validator.
# Sole author at present. ZoomzPeak is a PAASTA (Palaeoproteomics And
# Archaeology, Society for Techniques and Advances) initiative, and authorship
# is expected to broaden as the community contributes -- see CONTRIBUTING.md.
# Vocabulary bindings and archaeological context involve real scholarly
# judgement and are credited as authorship, not data entry.
authors:
  - family-names: Collins
    given-names: Matthew
    email: matthew@palaeome.org
    affiliation: "Palaeoprot / PAASTA"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Palaeoprot/ZoomzPeak"
url: "https://github.com/Palaeoprot/ZoomzPeak"
license: Apache-2.0
license-url: "https://github.com/Palaeoprot/ZoomzPeak/blob/main/LICENSE"
keywords:
  - PAASTA
  - ZooMS
  - palaeoproteomics
  - mass spectrometry
  - mzPeak
  - Parquet
  - controlled vocabulary
  - linked open data
  - archaeology
  - FAIR data
version: 0.0.0-pre
status: "pre-release — the specification is not yet stable"

# Vocabularies and standards this work builds on. Cite these alongside ZoomzPeak
# where you rely on them; mapping to a vocabulary does not replace citing it.
references:
